## Babau

A babau is a kind of demon, red-skinned and wet, dripping mucus, with a single bent horn low on the back of its head. It fights with a spear, and a wound from that spear bleeds and sickens and will not close. It can call down a darkness that leaves even those who see in the dark with nothing but shapes. When it is badly hurt it gushes a slime that burns.

Acid does nothing to it. Blessed weapons and cold iron cut it deeper than common steel. [[People/Sbrtlby Jotes|Sbrtlby Jotes]] is a babau.

## Barbazu

Barbazu are devils shaped like goat-men: horned, with the lower half of a goat and cloven hooves. They carry long glaives, and their beards move on their own and reach farther than the glaive does. A wound from a beard bleeds on and will not close, even after the fight is over. Fire does not burn them.

They can arrive in a burst of red smoke. Three fought beside a brimorak in the trial by combat at the [[Geography/Calaria/Ragged Roost|Ragged Roost]] pilgrimage, and all three are dead.

## Barghest

Barghests come out of the void, a cross between a dog and a long squirrel-like rodent, with a jaw full of teeth. They hunt in packs. They show no plan and go for whoever is nearest. A bite stains the flesh around it black and leaves a wound that will not close. Blessed weapons and cold iron cut them deeper than common steel, and they wither where holy power touches them. Their bodies go to pieces when someone tries to skin them, though a careful hand can keep a strip of the hide.

A pack poured out of the tear that opened in the [[Org/The Harlequins/Providence|Providence]]'s dance floor the night it left [[Geography/Calaria/Ragged Roost|Ragged Roost]]. Many were killed on the floor and some fled.

## Brimorak

Brimoraks are devils that carry a flaming sword and work fire. One breathes out its own burning blood in a line that knocks people from their feet. It can call down a ball of flame, and its own fire leaves it untouched.

The brimorak that fought beside two Barbazu in the trial by combat at the [[Geography/Calaria/Ragged Roost|Ragged Roost]] pilgrimage is dead, killed by Benny's pick.

## Corrupted Harlequin

A corrupted Harlequin is one of the [[Org/The Harlequins/index|Harlequins]], the pilgrimage's masked servants, bent out of humanoid shape. The joints sit at wrong angles, the back and torso are rearranged, and the mask has grown into the bone of the face and opens like a mouth. The costume peels open at the middle onto a purple void. It presses through a wall as if the wall were soft, and the floor dips under its weight and springs back. Beneath the skin is a hard shell, like chitin. Cold iron cuts one deeper than common steel, and magic aimed at the mind leaves it unmoved.

## Hellion

Hellions are small fiends with scaly red and yellow skin, claws, fangs and horns, and they travel in packs. They climb rock faster than a person can, and pour up through the cracks that open in a canyon wall.

A pack goes straight for the nearest body, trying to leap onto it, pry off armor and wrench a weapon from its hands. They fight as a mass rather than as separate warriors. Holy power scours them where ordinary cuts only thin them; a blessed strike passes through several at once. Threats do not move them.

A horde of them lives on the [[Geography/Star 221,325|Joker World at Star 221,325]].

## Ort

Orts are the least of the devils: soft, vaguely round blobs about three feet across that deform where they touch the ground, with five limbs, two to a side and one from the chest, and dents where eyes and mouth would be. They cannot yet think for themselves, and other fiends boss them about. A fiend stays an ort until it gathers enough power, given or taken, to take a truer form. [[Org/The Harlequins/index|Harlequins]] keep them as workers, walking them on leashes.

## Pusk

Pusks are demons that hire out as hands. They can push thoughts into the minds of those near them without speaking, and when frightened they make themselves small and hard to strike. When they die they burst apart into demon viscera.

Three of them, with two centipede-things, guarded the drug works at 414 Anchor Street in [[Geography/Calaria/Hallia/Deosil|Deosil]] for [[People/Sbrtlby Jotes|Sbrtlby Jotes]]. All three are dead.

## Rancorous Priest

Rancorous priests are fiends about seven feet tall and heavy-built, too large for the passages they travel. They contort themselves to squeeze through holes in a wall and pop out the other side. They wear robes, gather in troops, and chant hymns together.

Their chants call down divine wrath and void magic, and a full troop can drain a victim's blood to refill its own fallen. Holy power scours them. They fight alongside the Hellions in Sigzil Haight's demesne.

## Vitriolite

Vitriolites are winged, bat-like fiends. They carry weapons taken from elsewhere: one used a greataxe wreathed in flame, another a pistol it could fire without needing to aim. They teleport into a fight once they have had time to regroup, and they go straight for whoever is most exposed.

Two of them fought to keep the [[Org/The Scale/Voice of Many|Voice of Many]] in its chamber.
